{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-base-field-independence","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:base-field-independence","kind":"remark","title":"Base-ring independence","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-observable-universe"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-universe","tags":["foundations"],"text":"base-field-independence.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"rem:base-field-independence\"></a>\n<strong>Remark.</strong> <em>Base-ring independence</em></p>\n<p>Because these axioms are formulated categorically, the existence result holds over any commutative ring <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>, independent of archimedean, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>-adic, or finite-field realisations.</p>\n"}
